icon-key-table-iteration-order-differs-from-arizona-oracle
oplexgen emits JCON's operator-lexer decision tree by walking `every i := key(t.t)`
(oplexgen.icn:235,240,246,254). SCRIP's key(table) yields a different order than the
Arizona oracle's, so the generated tree is emitted in a different order. MEASURED
2026-09-03 (hq_B): 611 lines on both sides, `sort` of the two outputs is BYTE-IDENTICAL,
and m3 == m4 exactly -- the multiset of emitted lines agrees, only the order differs.
Icon does not specify key() order, so the generated source stays valid Icon either way;
this is a byte-identity gap against the oracle, not a wrong answer.
